::: {.doc-subject}

Plot Kaplan-Meier estimates on distribution-linearizing axes.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/feat-weibull-plots/greenwood/viz/_weibull.py#L105-L204){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
viz.plot_weibull(
    km,
    *,
    aft=None,
    dist="weibull",
    title=None,
    xlab=None,
    ylab=None,
    width=500,
    height=300
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Produces a diagnostic scatter plot of Kaplan-Meier survival estimates on transformed axes where
data from the specified parametric distribution falls on a straight line. This is the classic
"Weibull plot" (complementary log-log transform) generalized to other AFT distributions.

For stratified Kaplan-Meier fits, each stratum is drawn as a separate colored series. Parallel
lines indicate the proportional hazards assumption holds between groups.

An optional fitted `AFT` model overlays the theoretical parametric line on the empirical points,
showing goodness-of-fit visually. The overlay is available only for unstratified Kaplan-Meier
fits.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[km]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [KaplanMeier]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A fitted `KaplanMeier` object (stratified or unstratified).

<code>[aft]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   An optional fitted `AFT` model for a parametric overlay line. Only allowed with an
    unstratified `km`. The AFT's distribution must match the `dist` parameter (with
    `"exponential"` accepted when `dist="weibull"`).

<code>[dist]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;weibull&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Distribution whose linearizing transform is applied: `"weibull"` (default), `"lognormal"`,
    or `"loglogistic"`.

<code>[title]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Chart title. Defaults to `None` (no title).

<code>[xlab]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   X-axis label. Defaults to `"log(time)"`.

<code>[ylab]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Y-axis label. Defaults to a distribution-specific label.

<code>[width]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[500]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Chart dimensions in pixels (defaults 500 x 300).

<code>[height]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[500]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Chart dimensions in pixels (defaults 500 x 300).
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [altair.LayerChart]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   An interactive Altair chart.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

Check the Weibull assumption for lung cancer survival by sex:

::: {#09d405ca .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

lung = gw.load_dataset("lung", backend="polars")
y = gw.Surv.right(lung["time"], event=(lung["status"] == 2))

# Stratified KM where parallel lines suggest PH holds
km = gw.KaplanMeier().fit(y, by=lung["sex"])
gw.plot_weibull(km)
```

